## C4 diagram conventions

Architecture diagrams in proposals follow the C4 model. See `ea-practice/rfp-pursuit-guide.md` for full guidance.

**Which levels to produce per proposal:**

| Level | Required? | Content |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| C1 — System Context | Always | The proposed system and its external actors (users, external systems, integrations) |
| C2 — Container | Almost always | Major containers: applications, services, databases, messaging systems |
| C3 — Component | Selective | Internal components of a specific container — only when the RFP requires it or a key differentiator sits here |

**Rules:**
- Every diagram has a title, a legend, and a description of what it shows and what it intentionally omits.
- External systems are clearly distinguished from systems within scope.
- Diagram boundaries map to the SAD sections — no diagram should be unexplained by prose, no SAD section should be unrepresented in a diagram.
- Technology labels on containers and components match exactly what is named in the Technology Selection section.

